  {
   "k": "ta274u",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ ⟦1⟧ to attack and defense.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "bwcwr3",
   "en": "Amphibious landing:"
  },
  {
   "k": "1waqdr1",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ ⟦1⟧ to attack and defense per level of the fort, up to ⟦2⟧ at level 10.",
   "frags": 3
  },
  {
   "k": "1tjtuyq",
   "en": "Fort:"
  },
  {
   "k": "xa2tbo",
   "en": "The river adjuster applies when a path intersects a river. If a river modifier is applied in combat, this also enables certain ⟦0⟧.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "5nkwsk",
   "en": "combat tactics"
  },
  {
   "k": "x5mefs",
   "en": "The amphibious landing penalty applies when a unit attacks a land province from a sea province. It also applies on top of a multiplicative scaling modifier of ⟦0⟧⟦1⟧ to the attackers' soft and hard attack and ⟦2⟧⟦3⟧ to their breakthrough that slowly disappears over the course of combat.⟦4⟧ Both of these modifiers and the speed at which they disappear is affected by ⟦5⟧. The movement speed of a naval invasion is fixed to a speed of 3.557 km/h⟦6⟧⟦7⟧ that can be increased or decreased through division terrain modifiers.",
   "frags": 8
  },
  {
   "k": "ncho1k",
   "en": "transport technologies"
  },
  {
   "k": "1dys1ba",
   "en": "The fort adjuster applies to ⟦0⟧ in all directions, though not to ⟦1⟧. Flanking attacks diminish this penalty, with each additional direction of attacking reducing the effective level of a fort by 1 (i.e., effectively acting as a ⟦2⟧ adjuster). ⟦3⟧ reduce the attack when attacking in a ⟦4⟧ and when attacking across a strait.",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "1br9n7e",
